    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen004.png",
    "sha256": "006eac9e197dd74f840f456f5245dc8a563aef22c88d0aa0d5cb3c0b03430cea",
    "k": 3,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Antarctica, a continent of snow and ice, is now losing ice three times faster than it was in 2007.",
    "zh": "南极洲这片冰雪大陆，如今的冰流失速度达到了2007年的三倍。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Antarctica",
      "continent",
      "three times faster"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen005.png",
    "sha256": "2285b804fb4fe52883c320e5d0a376e6b315bf71206db87a4834862914ba70f2",
    "k": 4,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In a new study published last week in the journal Nature, ",
    "zh": "上周发表在《自然》杂志的一项新研究中，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "publish",
      "journal"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen006.png",
    "sha256": "9a7b7fd0bb696a0cbf815e78dd6316005e3b63f6a9d132afa6ea72b39be9247f",
    "k": 4,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "more than 80 scientists from multiple countries used satellite data to examine the Antarctica’s vast ice sheets, ",
    "zh": "来自多个国家的80多位科学家，利用卫星数据研究了南极广袤的冰盖；",
    "vocabulary": [
      "satellite data",
      "ice sheets"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen007.png",
    "sha256": "2b3e7d302bd885c8f661c5f6895f9114f40b3bfe8acd15d7a38724770ca98ffa",
    "k": 4,
    "part": 3,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "and their prediction is that if the current rate of ice melt continues, sea levels could rise six inches by the year 2100.",
    "zh": "他们预测，如果当前融冰速度持续下去，到2100年，海平面可能上升6英寸。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "prediction",
      "current rate"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen008.png",
    "sha256": "cf4d04efb041158983755b28ca0ddd99ec33f9478e2ecfcccc0450e7f9e89ded",
    "k": 5,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Joining us today for more on this study and the consequences of sea level rise is Benjamin Johnson, president and CEO of Climate Watch.",
    "zh": "今天，与我们进一步讨论这项研究及海平面上升后果的，是“气候观察”机构的总裁兼首席执行官本杰明·约翰逊。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "consequence",
      "sea level rise",
      "CEO"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen009.png",
    "sha256": "db2e740a710862a4169f1241c9f2556e1efd34a1d791e79f1cf329f0b4f9b3ed",
    "k": 6,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So Ben, we’ve heard about sea level rise for years.",
    "zh": "本，这些年来，我们一直听到有关海平面上升的消息。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "sea level rise"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen010.png",
    "sha256": "4407eb5905d055004b6c3d6ea092c8d1796c225341c3f0e7fccd6bc8df2d10d1",
    "k": 7,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "How significant is this particular study and what did it look at?",
    "zh": "这项研究到底有多重要，又研究了什么？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "significant",
      "look at"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen011.png",
    "sha256": "74a0919a6ab800918323f6487b85c07de1933b31c065b4372632fedd0405db25",
    "k": 8,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, the first thing I’d like to point out is Antarctica is just one part of the story.",
    "zh": "首先我想指出，南极洲只是整个问题的一部分。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "point out",
      "one part of the story"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen012.png",
    "sha256": "e03fe9b69fd9f56c7cc27a71db94a313fb7c748c77dd196c2f48771974c56eee",
    "k": 9,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "That is to say, we have six inches of contribution from Antarctica if it continues to shed ice at the rate it was measured.",
    "zh": "也就是说，如果南极洲继续以测得的速度流失冰层，它就会带来6英寸的海平面上升。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "contribution",
      "shed ice"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen013.png",
    "sha256": "2479dcb147bf632d60d1c861817185f17e24cffd559e145ee54599b9eca9b86c",
    "k": 10,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But, but there are other sources as well.",
    "zh": "但也还有其他来源。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "source"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen014.png",
    "sha256": "6822fa8dd50a86afc76843b00f6c4a9612846179e68896bbf194eb44cde144fe",
    "k": 11,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So altogether, we would be looking at three feet.",
    "zh": "所以总计来看，海平面可能上升3英尺。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "altogether",
      "three feet"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen015.png",
    "sha256": "3ea35dfd7723e9cb4b1b697c9a7ee00c608a3bf62c8d81d1f9015e76c6277f2e",
    "k": 12,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Three feet of sea level rise by the year 2100.",
    "zh": "到2100年，海平面上升3英尺。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "sea level rise"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen016.png",
    "sha256": "f4750c84b48704f7501a19f4672b324f9816e85a00954fb7012ef8cc427bee25",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "That is consequential to hundreds of millions of people that live in coastal cities all over the planet.",
    "zh": "这会对全球沿海城市中数以亿计的居民产生重大影响。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "consequential",
      "coastal cities"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen017.png",
    "sha256": "5e0a4a7c1ade46e16518a32e4e3bf571a8549ca3b580e76826e65714152e2b52",
    "k": 14,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Yes, it is. We’re already seeing floods increase.",
    "zh": "是的，确实如此。我们已经看到洪水在增多。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "flood"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen018.png",
    "sha256": "d727277d92cfb51a542148577e9bc8366372e0023598aa84126ed545f0b92937",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Yesterday, for example, there were huge floods in some of the areas around the country, ",
    "zh": "比如，昨天全国一些地区发生了严重洪水；",
    "vocabulary": [
      "flood"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen019.png",
    "sha256": "e34f754d35c424c0c22fb899775602deadddba19504237d3d87647cd2697b2ff",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "and these floods wouldn’t have happened without the sea level rise that we’ve already seen.",
    "zh": "如果没有我们已经经历的海平面上升，这些洪水本来不会发生。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "flood",
      "without",
      "sea level rise"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen020.png",
    "sha256": "bd84f05c70d3feb8118dbceb7eeaaeeb55be89c9d64b4531a5811fad2c11302f",
    "k": 16,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Yeah, and what is it that is convincing these scientists that the rates are changing?",
    "zh": "那么，究竟是什么让科学家们确信，上升的速度正在变化呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "convince",
      "rate"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen021.png",
    "sha256": "cc3017ceeedb00610d93ff372c49c624cc9ec951df298b2ac6b6fd37c7e5ce42",
    "k": 17,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What are they studying?",
    "zh": "他们在研究什么？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "study"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen022.png",
    "sha256": "73a56e43438ca5df260497d3998fe730a5dacb93dfc18c6d6c7b5ee3cbfc5fcc",
    "k": 18,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What are they looking at?",
    "zh": "他们在观察什么？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "look at"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen023.png",
    "sha256": "b61f54ec1c5ce6abba7c3a62c80ab6953369e495448378ea43a0080d1571c7fc",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "How can they tell?",
    "zh": "他们怎么判断呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "tell"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen024.png",
    "sha256": "8d982343a5b38c78087e48f37f10bbc6a5cc988907699fb1f7bf5aa32e19f2bc",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, they have a lot of direct measurements from satellites of the height of the surface of the ice sheets, ",
    "zh": "他们有大量卫星对冰盖表面高度的直接测量数据，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "direct measurements",
      "satellite"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen025.png",
    "sha256": "2374b3a31f5325591e34c2cc1bda214616d456904d349431ad16dbbbbceb282a",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "so they’re able to see how that height changes over time.",
    "zh": "因此能看出这些高度如何随时间变化。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "over time"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen026.png",
    "sha256": "f5cb927d98166e05b7e73aaa81cf91cc11520a8a865ba4ba9b5d341dc88d5558",
    "k": 21,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "These satellites also measure the gravitational pull of the ice sheet and, and therefore the scientists know how much ice is there.",
    "zh": "这些卫星也测量冰盖的引力，因此科学家能知道那里有多少冰。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "gravitational pull"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen027.png",
    "sha256": "8e6a6b90868dbe1dd1111b46952e21a1e6db4d8509e2278832be792101de6763",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So those are the two main forms of measurement.",
    "zh": "这就是两种主要的测量方式。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "measurement"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen028.png",
    "sha256": "426bb1676879eaffbda511cded0a1d8d244201be0b7185e6dbdc3346fc8a87ea",
    "k": 23,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I know that there are climate science deniers who say “look at the east side of Antarctica, it looks on a map, there’s actually more ice coming in.”",
    "zh": "我知道有些气候科学否认者会说：“看看南极洲东部，从地图上看，那里的冰实际上还在增加。”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "climate science",
      "denier"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen029.png",
    "sha256": "a8d9617304c956c06f24a4ec41edc6f19afda6e039eac5d58807deb3fae5fe55",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Doesn’t this all balance itself out?",
    "zh": "这些增减难道不会相互抵消吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "balance out"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen030.png",
    "sha256": "b6a3709f2ef802c209263f0b5615c0e3e84baa85be371e5d66d14361b077aa2c",
    "k": 25,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We do anticipate that in the future, snowfall will increase in East Antarctica and I hope so.",
    "zh": "我们确实预计，未来东南极洲的降雪会增加，我也希望如此。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "anticipate",
      "snowfall"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen031.png",
    "sha256": "5f2a1fb77f128350ccd7d67ebd54742d2bb7b54614346f65eaa2bab2d2dcfda5",
    "k": 26,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But this study shows over recent decades it hasn’t.",
    "zh": "但这项研究表明，近几十年来并没有出现这种情况。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "decade"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen032.png",
    "sha256": "3224fcba6430d9d258cae3e70c063cadccd0d69db961297e0b67e8e4298befa0",
    "k": 27,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Does it mean that if nothing is going to change, areas around on coastal waterways will be severely impacted?",
    "zh": "这是否意味着，如果情况毫无改变，沿海水道周边地区就会受到严重影响？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "coastal waterways",
      "severely",
      "impact"
    ]
  },
  {
